---
import { patchwork, type Patchwork } from "../../data/site";

// One glyph per kind of artifact. Six identical pills said "six things"; a
// spreadsheet, a paper cuaderno and a chat thread say what KIND of mess it is,
// which is the part a director recognises as their own Friday afternoon.
const GLYPHS: Record<Patchwork, string[]> = {
  sheet: ["M4.5 3.5h15v17h-15z", "M4.5 9h15", "M4.5 14.5h15", "M11 9v11.5"],
  paper: ["M6 3.5h7.5l4.5 4.5v12H6z", "M13.5 3.5V8H18", "M9 12h6", "M9 16h4"],
  chat: ["M4 5.5h16v10.5h-9l-5 4v-4H4z", "M8 9h8", "M8 12.5h5"],
};
---

<section class="band pain fold-band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="narrow reveal">
      <h2>El cierre de periodo, sin armar nada a mano.</h2>
      <p>
        Las notas viven en el archivo de Excel de cada docente. La asistencia,
        en papel. Los encargados preguntan por WhatsApp. Y al cierre de cada
        periodo alguien en la dirección junta todo eso, hoja por hoja, para
        poder entregar notas a tiempo.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="contrast">
      <div class="side">
        <p class="side-label">Cómo se hace hoy</p>
        <ul class="scatter reveal reveal-stagger">
          {
            patchwork.map((p, i) => (
              <li style={`--i:${i}`}>
                <svg class="glyph" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                  {GLYPHS[p.kind].map((d) => (
                    <path d={d} />
                  ))}
                </svg>
                <span class="scatter-text">
                  <span class="scatter-name">{p.label}</span>
                  <span class="scatter-meta">{p.meta}</span>
                </span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- A glyph sized to itself, not a shape stretched across a column.
           Decorative: the two labels either side already say it. -->
      <div class="turn reveal" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="turn-badge">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path d="M4 12h15M13 5.5 19.5 12 13 18.5"></path>
          </svg>
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="side">
        <p class="side-label">Cómo se hace con Simple Manage Pro</p>

        <!-- The same six sheets, squared into one stack. The two layers behind
             the card are the rest of the pile: they start scattered and settle
             flush as the section arrives, which is the collapse the section is
             arguing for. Gated behind .js, which Layout.astro adds only when
             the visitor has not asked for reduced motion, so a reduced-motion
             or no-JavaScript visitor gets the settled stack rather than a pile
             frozen mid-fall. -->
        <div class="stack reveal">
          <span class="sheet sheet-2" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="sheet sheet-1" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="card-lead one">
            <p class="one-title">Un solo sistema</p>
            <p class="one-body">
              Las mismas notas, la misma asistencia y la misma matrícula, en un
              solo lugar y actualizadas por quien las tiene de primera mano.
            </p>
            <ul class="streams">
              <li class="chip">Notas</li>
              <li class="chip">Asistencia</li>
              <li class="chip">Matrícula</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="narrow reveal">
      <p class="aside">
        Simple Manage Pro no reemplaza nada del MEP. Ordena la información que
        el colegio ya maneja por dentro.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .contrast {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    align-items: center;
    margin-block: var(--space-5);
  }

  .side-label {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-info-dark);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  /* ── The six sources ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  .scatter {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }

  .scatter li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.4rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--color-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-light);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius-2);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    box-shadow: var(--elev-1);
    /* Each row sits at its own small angle. The point is legibility of the
       mess, not the mess itself: they stay readable, just visibly unaligned. */
    rotate: var(--tilt, 0deg);
  }
  .scatter li:nth-child(1) {
    --tilt: -1.4deg;
  }
  .scatter li:nth-child(2) {
    --tilt: 0.9deg;
  }
  .scatter li:nth-child(3) {
    --tilt: -0.6deg;
  }
  .scatter li:nth-child(4) {
    --tilt: 1.5deg;
  }
  .scatter li:nth-child(5) {
    --tilt: -1.1deg;
  }
  .scatter li:nth-child(6) {
    --tilt: 0.7deg;
  }

  /* `rotate` rather than `transform` above, so the stagger's translateY and
     this angle do not fight over the same property. */
  .glyph {
    width: 1.4rem;
    height: 1.4rem;
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-info-dark);
    stroke-width: 1.6;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .scatter-name {
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-dark);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .scatter-meta {
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-info-dark);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  /* ── The turn ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  .turn {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    min-height: 3rem;
  }

  .turn-badge {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2.6rem;
    height: 2.6rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-light);
    box-shadow: var(--elev-1);
  }

  .turn-badge svg {
    width: 1.3rem;
    height: 1.3rem;
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-primary-text);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    rotate: 90deg;
  }

  /* ── The one system ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  /* The sheets sit 1.2rem above the card's own box, so the stack needs that
     back as clearance or the top edge of the pile touches the label. */
  .stack {
    position: relative;
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }

  /* The rest of the pile, showing only as edges behind the top card. */
  .sheet {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    border-radius: var(--card-border-radius);
    background: var(--color-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-light);
    box-shadow: var(--elev-1);
  }
  .sheet-1 {
    translate: -0.6rem -0.6rem;
    rotate: -1.2deg;
  }
  .sheet-2 {
    translate: -1.2rem -1.2rem;
    rotate: -2.6deg;
  }

  .js .sheet {
    transition:
      translate var(--dur-slow) var(--ease-out),
      rotate var(--dur-slow) var(--ease-out);
  }
  /* Scattered until the section arrives. The top card never moves, so the
     collapse reads as loose sheets being squared up against it. */
  .js .stack:not(.is-in) .sheet-1 {
    translate: -2.6rem -1.9rem;
    rotate: -6deg;
  }
  .js .stack:not(.is-in) .sheet-2 {
    translate: -4.4rem 0.9rem;
    rotate: 5.5deg;
  }
  .js .stack .sheet-2 {
    transition-delay: 90ms;
  }

  .one {
    --accent: var(--color-primary-fill);
    position: relative;
  }
  .one-title {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-dark);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .one-body {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }
  .streams {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .contrast {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-4);
    }
    .scatter {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
    .turn-badge svg {
      rotate: none;
    }
    .wedge {
      clip-path: polygon(0 4%, 100% 40%, 100% 60%, 0 96%);
    }
    .tip {
      rotate: none;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .scatter li {
      rotate: none;
    }
    .js .sheet {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
